  "title": "13 survivors from an 1898 ship that predicted Titanic",
  "description": "Morgan Robertson’s novel *Futility* described a fictional liner, the Titan, that sank after striking an iceberg in 1898. Fourteen years later, the real Titanic met the same fate, sparking speculation of prophetic foresight.\n\nKey points:\n• 1898 novel warned of an iceberg collision and insufficient lifeboats.\n• Only thirteen survivors were reported.\n• The book was reissued after Titanic’s wreck, highlighting uncanny parallels.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"The Wreck of the Titan: Or, Futility\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Titan:_Or,_Futility), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nRoman mount in the form of a panther emerging from a flower, close up (FindID 89170-53280).jpg (Colchester Museums, Caroline McDonald, 2006-03-29 13:21:14, CC BY-SA 2.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_mount_in_the_form_of_a_panther_emerging_from_a_flower,_close_up_(FindID_89170-53280).jpg\nTitan-crystal bar.JPG (Alchemist-hp ( pse-mendelejew.de ), CC BY-SA 3.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titan-crystal_bar.JPG\nTitan in true color by Kevin M. Gill.jpg (NASA/JPL-Caltech/SSI/Kevin M. Gill, CC BY 2.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titan_in_true_color_by_Kevin_M._Gill.jpg\nVince Zampella.jpg (Dean Takahashi, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vince_Zampella.jpg\nSaturn during Equinox.jpg (NASA / JPL / Space Science Institute, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_during_Equinox.jpg\nRoman mount in the form of a panther emerging from a flower, close up (FindID 89170-53280).jpg (Colchester Museums, Caroline McDonald, 2006-03-29 13:21:14, CC BY-SA 2.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_mount_in_the_form_of_a_panther_emerging_from_a_flower,_close_up_(FindID_89170-53280).jpg\nTitan Missile Family.png (Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titan_Missile_Family.png\nTitán (wrestler).jpg (ゾーヒョー, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tit%C3%A1n_(wrestler).jpg\nWreck and sinking of the Titanic - the ocean's greatest disaster - a graphic and thrilling account of the sinking of the greatest floating palace ever built, carrying down to watery graves more than (14593187138).jpg (Internet Archive Book Images, No restrictions): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wreck_and_sinking_of_the_Titanic_-_the_ocean%27s_greatest_disaster_-_a_graphic_and_thrilling_account_of_the_sinking_of_the_greatest_floating_palace_ever_built,_carrying_down_to_watery_graves_more_than_(14593187138).jpg\nGustave Doré - Dante Alighieri - Inferno - Plate 65 (Canto XXXI - The Titans).jpg (Gustave Doré (1832 – 1883), Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustave_Dor%C3%A9_-_Dante_Alighieri_-_Inferno_-_Plate_65_(Canto_XXXI_-_The_Titans).jpg\n\n3D models:\nShip in Clouds by Bastien Genbrugge (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-c475323dc7f24e26ba2009c08c8e1941",
